WEBVTT

01:47.300 --> 01:51.940
[Mystic Nine]
[Adapted from the novel of Kennedy Xu]

01:52.130 --> 01:55.050
[Episode 20]
[This story is purely fictional]

02:01.020 --> 02:04.220
[Artifact Chest]

02:04.660 --> 02:06.820
[Artifact Chest]

02:10.590 --> 02:12.540
Only two lots remain.

02:23.080 --> 02:24.980
Our funds are only enough to bid on one chest.

02:25.190 --> 02:26.540
We'll have to get someone else to win one of them.

02:27.400 --> 02:29.170
The first chest must go to a Chinese bidder.

02:29.910 --> 02:31.980
Tian Zuocheng is new money.

02:32.120 --> 02:33.380
He made his fortune recently, and he's hot-tempered.

02:34.240 --> 02:36.010
What he fears most is being looked down on.

02:36.470 --> 02:38.340
He can't stand being upstaged.

02:38.960 --> 02:39.890
All you have to do

02:39.910 --> 02:41.170
is pose as an opium merchant from the south.

02:41.430 --> 02:42.660
Act more arrogant than he is.

02:42.910 --> 02:44.100
Throw money around even more lavishly.

02:44.800 --> 02:46.610
Once he feels his pride has been challenged,

02:47.280 --> 02:47.940
he'll lose his temper.

02:49.030 --> 02:49.850
We have to make sure

02:49.870 --> 02:51.410
he wins one of the chests.

02:52.120 --> 02:53.660
Once it's transported out of Beiping,

02:54.280 --> 02:55.850
intercept it on the road.

03:08.840 --> 03:09.380
Ladies and gentlemen,

03:10.120 --> 03:12.170
we've now come to

03:12.560 --> 03:14.980
tonight's grand finale.

03:16.080 --> 03:19.130
A pair of artifact chests from the remote mountains of Xiangxi.

03:22.400 --> 03:24.890
Legend has it that each chest contains an ascended mummy.

03:25.630 --> 03:27.890
Ancient texts say the ascended mummy

03:28.000 --> 03:30.890
is a relic left behind by an immortal of antiquity.

03:31.400 --> 03:33.540
Whoever obtains it can avert calamities,

03:33.590 --> 03:34.730
extend their lifespan,

03:34.960 --> 03:36.660
or reverse life and death.

03:37.000 --> 03:38.260
Its mysteries are beyond measure.

03:39.240 --> 03:41.410
But legends are only legends.

03:41.750 --> 03:42.820
Whether they're real or not is anyone's guess.

03:43.080 --> 03:44.940
Their value lies in the eye of the beholder.

03:46.080 --> 03:48.450
The opening bid is 50,000 silver coins.

03:49.960 --> 03:51.040
We have to get this one.

03:51.040 --> 03:51.970
We can't let it slip away.

03:55.000 --> 03:57.940
What do you think of this lot, Miss Huo?

04:01.870 --> 04:03.940
Are you saying the Empire of Japan

04:04.560 --> 04:05.660
isn't worthy of owning it?

04:06.400 --> 04:08.170
It's an artifact from the Miao and Yao regions of Xiangxi.

04:09.280 --> 04:11.410
It has nothing to do with your country's cultural interests.

04:11.840 --> 04:12.660
Why bother bidding on it?

04:13.520 --> 04:14.410
It's too niche.

04:14.800 --> 04:15.780
You could end up holding the bag.

04:16.120 --> 04:18.020
I think it's worth joining the bidding.

04:18.830 --> 04:19.730
Miss Huo,

04:20.190 --> 04:22.020
are you asking me to give it up?

04:29.120 --> 04:32.020
Are you hiding something from me?

04:36.720 --> 04:38.610
How can I be your adviser if you don't trust me?

04:44.160 --> 04:45.540
Bid however you like.

04:45.630 --> 04:46.170
Very well.

05:07.680 --> 05:10.660
The bidding begins now.

05:11.040 --> 05:11.980
100,000.

05:14.030 --> 05:15.330
Who's that?

05:18.160 --> 05:18.810
Raise your paddle.

05:24.000 --> 05:24.660
100,000.

05:33.600 --> 05:34.340
Everyone,

05:35.120 --> 05:36.930
I know the rules say that anyone who failed to win three lots

05:37.600 --> 05:39.100
can't bid in the late session.

05:39.720 --> 05:40.900
But allow me to make my case.

05:42.360 --> 05:44.540
I'm an opium merchant from Jiangxi.

05:45.240 --> 05:46.540
I've only just arrived in Beiping.

05:47.190 --> 05:50.140
If anyone plans to do opium business in the future, remember my name.

05:51.070 --> 05:52.460
Tonight, I'm using this auction

05:52.630 --> 05:53.810
to introduce myself.

05:54.270 --> 05:56.730
That artifact chest is mine.

05:57.560 --> 05:58.980
Whoever lends me two of the earlier lots,

06:00.480 --> 06:02.020
I'll give them this artifact chest as interest

06:03.040 --> 06:04.370
once I win it.

06:06.360 --> 06:06.900
Really?

06:09.120 --> 06:09.700
I'll lend him one.

06:09.800 --> 06:10.490
Me too.

06:19.510 --> 06:20.340
We've got

06:21.310 --> 06:22.340
plenty of money.

06:25.800 --> 06:28.250
So I hope the private boxes upstairs

06:28.600 --> 06:29.580
won't place a blanket bid.

06:30.070 --> 06:32.580
Please give those of us in the main hall a chance.

06:38.830 --> 06:41.020
Who does this nobody think he is?

06:42.390 --> 06:43.460
150,000.

06:45.120 --> 06:47.540
Private Room No. 2 bids 150,000.

06:51.270 --> 06:52.290
170,000.

06:52.680 --> 06:55.050
Private Room No. 1 bids 170,000.

06:58.870 --> 06:59.660
200,000.

06:59.950 --> 07:02.460
Table 13 bids 200,000.

07:04.510 --> 07:05.660
250,000.

07:06.240 --> 07:09.020
Private Room No. 1 bids 250,000.

07:11.320 --> 07:13.240
- What a big spender. - Exactly.

07:15.360 --> 07:16.290
260,000.

07:17.360 --> 07:18.170
Sir,

07:18.800 --> 07:20.780
you've reached your credit limit.

07:21.430 --> 07:24.250
Will you be using the money in your deposit chest?

07:24.560 --> 07:26.220
Shall I have someone bring it over for verification?

07:26.220 --> 07:27.840
He even brings his entire fortune.

07:27.840 --> 07:29.070
Exactly.

08:06.600 --> 08:07.460
Sir,

08:07.870 --> 08:09.370
if you're unable to provide additional funds,

08:09.720 --> 08:11.410
the highest valid bid remains

08:11.430 --> 08:12.730
Private Room No. 1's 250,000.

08:14.800 --> 08:16.340
250,000, going once.

08:17.190 --> 08:18.370
Any higher bids?

08:21.680 --> 08:23.220
250,000, going twice.

08:27.000 --> 08:27.730
Miss Huo,

08:28.240 --> 08:29.810
this treasure is beyond the reach of ordinary people.

08:30.040 --> 08:31.660
Only the Empire of Japan

08:32.720 --> 08:34.010
deserves it.

08:41.390 --> 08:42.650
250,000...

08:42.960 --> 08:43.530
Everyone,

08:44.240 --> 08:46.420
we've got two tons of opium

08:47.630 --> 08:49.010
that just arrived in Beiping today.

08:49.360 --> 08:50.250
It hasn't been sold yet.

08:51.150 --> 08:52.530
Will the Xinyue Restaurant

08:52.840 --> 08:55.530
accept opium as collateral?

08:56.670 --> 08:57.250
No.

08:57.750 --> 09:00.060
That's never been our policy.

09:00.670 --> 09:02.730
You should think carefully.

09:03.150 --> 09:04.530
Soon, I'll be supplying all the opium

09:05.000 --> 09:06.490
in Beiping.

09:06.960 --> 09:08.100
One month's profit

09:08.480 --> 09:10.250
would be enough to buy this entire restaurant.

09:11.870 --> 09:12.820
Sir,

09:13.510 --> 09:15.650
the Xinyue Restaurant does not accept opium.

09:21.080 --> 09:21.730
Everyone,

09:23.270 --> 09:24.530
do you want opium?

09:25.440 --> 09:26.610
I'm going all in today.

09:27.670 --> 09:30.100
I've got two tons of top-grade opium as collateral.

09:31.000 --> 09:32.730
If anyone here is willing

09:32.790 --> 09:33.580
to lend me money,

09:34.870 --> 09:37.940
I'll settle it at 100 silver coins per jin.

09:38.720 --> 09:40.060
- One hundred?
- But only during this auction.

09:41.120 --> 09:42.420
Think it over.

09:43.080 --> 09:45.770
Once this chance is gone, it's gone for good.

09:46.510 --> 09:47.580
One hundred silver coins.

09:48.120 --> 09:49.890
Even ordinary opium

09:50.240 --> 09:51.530
sells for at least 200 silver coins a jin

09:51.750 --> 09:53.060
these days.

09:53.480 --> 09:55.250
Exactly. That's half price.

09:55.510 --> 09:56.370
It's a bargain.

09:56.630 --> 09:58.580
Opium is in short supply in Beiping right now.

09:58.870 --> 10:00.820
At that price, he may as well be giving it away.

10:01.390 --> 10:02.010
Do you want it?

10:02.200 --> 10:02.820
Of course.

10:02.940 --> 10:03.490
Yeah.

10:03.490 --> 10:04.690
- Who wouldn't? - I want it.

10:04.870 --> 10:06.490
Master, you can't do this.

10:06.840 --> 10:07.980
If you sell at that price,

10:08.120 --> 10:09.370
every opium dealer in Beiping

10:09.670 --> 10:11.340
will blame us for undercutting the market.

10:12.600 --> 10:15.220
Soon there won't be any dealers left.

10:15.670 --> 10:17.010
Once they try my product,

10:17.600 --> 10:19.250
they'll never buy from anyone else again.

10:19.480 --> 10:21.730
Come on, everyone.

10:22.750 --> 10:25.580
If you want it, bring me your money now.

10:26.750 --> 10:28.180
- I want some! - Me too!

10:34.030 --> 10:36.460
Master, they're making a big scene.

10:36.960 --> 10:38.770
Looks like they're trying to build a reputation

10:39.480 --> 10:41.850
using this auction.

10:42.120 --> 10:44.130
Could they be after our business?

10:45.200 --> 10:46.770
Should we put them in their place?

10:51.240 --> 10:52.340
The fortune teller warned me

10:53.150 --> 10:54.820
that my luck is clashing this month.

10:55.670 --> 10:57.770
He told me to stay calm and not act rashly.

10:59.440 --> 11:00.100
Let's wait and see.

11:09.440 --> 11:10.220
300,000.

11:10.480 --> 11:12.610
Table 13 bids 300,000.

11:13.720 --> 11:14.980
My friend from Jiangxi,

11:15.630 --> 11:17.490
you don't look like you're here to buy antiques.

11:18.630 --> 11:20.100
You look like you're here to seize territory.

11:23.790 --> 11:25.250
Times have changed.

11:25.840 --> 11:26.730
When it's time to step aside,

11:27.360 --> 11:29.730
you should step aside.

11:30.790 --> 11:32.130
You're certainly making a grand entrance.

11:32.550 --> 11:33.220
I'm just wondering

11:33.240 --> 11:35.650
if you can really afford to back it up.

11:36.200 --> 11:37.700
After all, you're spending borrowed money.

11:38.120 --> 11:38.700
Of course,

11:39.320 --> 11:40.580
these days are hard.

11:41.030 --> 11:42.490
Even Beiping's opium dealers

11:42.670 --> 11:45.130
might not be able to scrape together that much money.

11:46.000 --> 11:47.250
I'm nothing like

11:47.270 --> 11:48.340
you Beiping dealers.

11:48.630 --> 11:49.730
You call yourselves

11:50.080 --> 11:51.730
the Opium Emperor,

11:51.840 --> 11:52.890
the Opium King,

11:53.510 --> 11:55.610
but your pockets have actually nothing but loose change.

11:56.790 --> 11:58.180
Let me make one thing clear.

11:58.910 --> 12:02.180
Sooner or later, the opium trade in Beiping will belong to me.

12:04.150 --> 12:05.250
From then on,

12:05.790 --> 12:07.060
I'll be calling the shots here.

12:07.480 --> 12:10.340
And this artifact chest is mine.

12:12.390 --> 12:13.420
350,000.

12:16.720 --> 12:19.650
Private Room No. 2 bids 350,000.

12:31.320 --> 12:32.250
380,000.

12:32.360 --> 12:34.980
Table 13 bids 380,000.

12:35.030 --> 12:36.010
400,000.

12:36.600 --> 12:37.700
430,000.

12:38.270 --> 12:39.250
450,000.

12:39.320 --> 12:39.850
Miss Huo.

12:39.870 --> 12:40.730
470,000.

12:40.790 --> 12:42.530
- What should we do? - 500,000.

12:42.750 --> 12:43.850
As matters stand,

12:44.510 --> 12:45.370
it may look

12:45.550 --> 12:46.650
like they're driving up the price.

12:47.270 --> 12:48.130
But in reality,

12:48.910 --> 12:50.180
they're gambling everything they own

12:50.600 --> 12:52.250
to fight for their business and reputation.

12:53.270 --> 12:55.180
This is bound to end in mutual ruin.

12:55.720 --> 12:58.060
Well said, Miss Huo.

13:01.510 --> 13:02.580
Stop bidding.

13:02.840 --> 13:03.890
No matter who wins

13:03.960 --> 13:05.370
this chest,

13:06.120 --> 13:07.460
we'll still have another chance.

13:08.030 --> 13:10.340
I'll contact Beiping's underworld immediately

13:10.510 --> 13:12.300
and have them seize the chest.

13:12.440 --> 13:13.100
Hurry.

13:13.200 --> 13:13.650
Yes, sir.

13:21.670 --> 13:24.460
I bid 600,000.

13:25.270 --> 13:28.060
Private Room No. 2 bids 600,000.

13:31.630 --> 13:33.010
600,000, going once.

13:34.910 --> 13:37.100
600,000, going twice.

13:39.240 --> 13:41.300
600,000, going three times.

13:45.240 --> 13:46.490
It goes to the highest bidder.

13:46.750 --> 13:49.420
Congratulations, Mr. Tian.

14:06.600 --> 14:07.820
Master,

14:08.510 --> 14:10.180
we're almost out of money.

14:10.480 --> 14:11.340
That's enough.

14:11.840 --> 14:13.850
We've made our name tonight.

14:14.320 --> 14:15.300
Tomorrow, my name

14:15.510 --> 14:16.340
will be on the front page

14:16.480 --> 14:17.890
of every newspaper in Beiping.

14:18.120 --> 14:19.370
The whole city will know who I am.

14:20.910 --> 14:21.370
Go.

14:22.120 --> 14:22.770
Pay the bill,

14:23.120 --> 14:24.580
collect the chest, and let's leave.

14:25.120 --> 14:25.530
Yes, master.

14:30.600 --> 14:32.010
Pay everyone back, and we're out.

14:41.390 --> 14:41.940
Jiu.

14:44.910 --> 14:46.060
One more chest left.

14:46.510 --> 14:47.250
Hang in there.

15:10.750 --> 15:12.890
This is tonight's final lot.

15:15.120 --> 15:16.130
Other than the color,

15:16.360 --> 15:17.820
it's almost identical to the previous chest.

15:18.320 --> 15:19.940
Looks like this one's going to fetch an astronomical price too.

15:21.720 --> 15:22.650
Inside this chest

15:22.810 --> 15:24.010
lies an ascended mummy.

15:24.440 --> 15:25.730
A treasure rarely seen in this world,

15:26.080 --> 15:27.250
a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

15:28.030 --> 15:29.530
If you miss it tonight,

15:29.670 --> 15:31.220
even a fortune beyond measure

15:31.390 --> 15:33.010
may never buy you another chance.

15:33.750 --> 15:36.180
Don't let this final opportunity slip away.

15:36.720 --> 15:38.850
The bidding starts now.

15:47.630 --> 15:50.060
I bid 300,000.

15:51.360 --> 15:53.770
Private Room No. 1 bids 300,000.

15:57.480 --> 15:58.980
Any higher bids?

16:02.750 --> 16:04.370
300,000, going once.

16:06.840 --> 16:08.700
300,000, going twice.

16:13.030 --> 16:13.940
300,000,

16:14.000 --> 16:15.060
- going three...
- Place the blanket bid.

16:18.910 --> 16:21.490
Private Room No. 5 places a blanket bid.

16:22.390 --> 16:22.940
President,

16:23.670 --> 16:24.700
"Blanket Bidding" at an auction

16:24.790 --> 16:26.130
means covering the entire sale.

16:26.390 --> 16:27.530
No matter how high the bidding goes,

16:27.960 --> 16:29.850
the blanket bidder pays the final price.

16:30.910 --> 16:32.460
Liang Bencai is making sure no one else stands a chance.

16:32.960 --> 16:34.180
What is he trying to do?

16:37.630 --> 16:38.370
You can't place a blanket bid!

16:40.600 --> 16:41.300
Liang Bencai,

16:41.960 --> 16:42.980
what gives you the right?

16:44.000 --> 16:45.490
You're spending our money.

16:45.750 --> 16:46.890
How dare you make this decision on your own?

16:47.440 --> 16:48.370
Take it down!

16:48.480 --> 16:49.100
Now!

16:57.720 --> 16:58.980
President Tottori,

16:59.720 --> 17:02.700
the ascended mummy is a relic left by our Chinese ancestors.

17:03.390 --> 17:05.570
I will never allow the Japanese to take it

17:05.920 --> 17:06.700
and carry it overseas.

17:08.240 --> 17:11.010
I'm placing this blanket bid today, no matter what.

17:18.750 --> 17:20.570
Freeze every account under his name.

17:21.030 --> 17:22.460
Don't let him spend another cent.

17:22.640 --> 17:23.140
Yes, sir.

17:24.440 --> 17:25.090
Be my guest.

17:25.750 --> 17:29.180
The funds we used for verification didn't come from your government.

17:31.030 --> 17:34.290
The account verified by the Xinyue Restaurant belongs to a private local bank.

17:34.510 --> 17:36.220
It has no connection to Japan.

17:36.400 --> 17:36.980
Punk!

17:37.200 --> 17:39.380
Punk!

17:47.270 --> 17:50.980
That Liang Bencai must be an impostor.

17:52.160 --> 17:53.860
Count every cent we have.

17:54.070 --> 17:56.010
We must win that artifact chest.

17:56.110 --> 17:56.570
Yes, sir.

17:59.000 --> 18:00.140
Isn't Liang Bencai

18:00.640 --> 18:02.180
the chief editor of Yahe Monthly?

18:02.790 --> 18:04.700
That magazine is funded by the Japanese.

18:05.160 --> 18:07.010
He has been helping the Japanese

18:07.030 --> 18:07.980
with all kinds of shady business.

18:08.830 --> 18:10.420
So why is he suddenly

18:10.550 --> 18:11.530
standing against them today?

18:12.270 --> 18:13.680
- Exactly. - That's right.

18:13.680 --> 18:14.200
Yeah.

18:14.200 --> 18:17.460
Yes, Yahe Monthly is funded by the Japanese.

18:18.030 --> 18:19.330
I've never denied that.

18:20.310 --> 18:21.250
But precisely because of that,

18:21.920 --> 18:23.140
we've seen how they've used archaeology

18:23.160 --> 18:23.900
as an excuse

18:24.550 --> 18:25.530
to ship our cultural relics, ancient books,

18:25.550 --> 18:27.380
and stone inscriptions overseas,

18:28.400 --> 18:29.010
cart after cart,

18:29.790 --> 18:30.860
ship after ship,

18:31.000 --> 18:32.940
over those years.

18:34.480 --> 18:36.010
The ascended mummy is no ordinary relic.

18:37.270 --> 18:38.220
I will never allow

18:38.680 --> 18:40.700
our national treasures to leave Chinese soil.

18:41.400 --> 18:43.180
Otherwise, I'd have no face to face my ancestors.

18:44.350 --> 18:47.250
Today, I will win this artifact chest.

18:48.000 --> 18:49.530
- Exactly! - Well said!

18:49.550 --> 18:52.180
- Well said! - Well said!

18:53.030 --> 18:53.530
That's right!

18:54.000 --> 18:55.380
- We can't let the Japanese have it.
- Right!

18:55.440 --> 18:56.500
- Chief Editor Liang is right!
- Never let it fall into Japanese hands!

18:56.550 --> 18:56.930
Exactly!

18:56.960 --> 18:57.460
Well said!

18:57.880 --> 19:00.380
Private Room No. 5 has placed a blanket bid.

19:01.310 --> 19:03.460
Any higher bids?

19:10.440 --> 19:11.770
If there are none,

19:12.030 --> 19:13.900
this artifact chest belongs to Liang...

19:13.920 --> 19:15.290
Place the blanket bid!

19:19.350 --> 19:22.010
Private Room No. 1 places a blanket bid.

19:28.310 --> 19:31.090
I'd like to see just how deep your pockets are

19:31.830 --> 19:33.620
to make you so confident.

19:47.480 --> 19:47.940
President,

19:48.550 --> 19:50.380
our available funds total one million.

19:50.960 --> 19:51.460
Yes.

20:12.000 --> 20:12.810
Miss Huo,

20:13.200 --> 20:14.730
do you still advise

20:15.480 --> 20:16.290
against bidding?

20:17.270 --> 20:19.570
It's your money. Spend it however you like.

20:20.310 --> 20:21.250
Buy

20:22.070 --> 20:23.530
whichever item you want.

20:24.590 --> 20:26.250
Besides, this is the final lot.

20:27.680 --> 20:28.900
Once this auction ends,

20:29.070 --> 20:30.290
you'll give me all of my antidote?

20:30.480 --> 20:31.250
Of course.

20:32.240 --> 20:35.050
What exactly is the ascended mummy for?

20:41.880 --> 20:44.900
Xiangu said the Japanese still have another million.

20:45.640 --> 20:46.620
We can risk it.

20:49.510 --> 20:51.940
I bid 500,000.

20:51.960 --> 20:53.810
Private Room No. 1 bids 500,000.

20:54.160 --> 20:55.010
Five hundred thousand?

20:55.440 --> 20:57.290
How did the price jump that high right away?

20:57.830 --> 20:58.700
800,000.

20:58.790 --> 21:00.530
Private Room No. 5 bids 800,000.

21:00.790 --> 21:01.730
830,000.

21:01.790 --> 21:03.700
Private Room No. 1 bids 830,000.

21:03.830 --> 21:04.900
One million.

21:05.110 --> 21:07.330
Private Room No. 5 bids one million.

21:08.790 --> 21:09.420
President,

21:09.830 --> 21:11.140
we're almost at our limit.

21:11.550 --> 21:12.860
Requesting more funds from the Empire will take time.

21:12.920 --> 21:14.090
1.05 million.

21:14.750 --> 21:17.620
Private Room No. 1 bids 1.05 million.

21:19.160 --> 21:19.620
President.

21:21.830 --> 21:23.290
I have personal funds.

21:23.400 --> 21:24.380
It's enough to keep us going.

21:25.110 --> 21:25.660
Continue.

21:26.030 --> 21:26.570
Yes, sir.

21:30.070 --> 21:31.180
1.1 million.

21:31.310 --> 21:32.180
1.2 million.

21:32.270 --> 21:33.050
1.3 million.

21:33.160 --> 21:34.420
1.35 million.

21:34.510 --> 21:35.420
1.4 million.

21:35.750 --> 21:37.220
I'm sorry, Chief Editor Liang.

21:37.920 --> 21:39.660
You've reached the limit of your guaranteed funds.

21:40.110 --> 21:41.570
If you wish to continue bidding,

21:41.720 --> 21:43.330
you'll need to provide additional funds.

21:43.750 --> 21:45.980
Otherwise, you'll be forced to withdraw.

21:56.920 --> 21:57.770
Think of something.

22:00.310 --> 22:01.770
Mr. Liang, I've got 50,000.

22:01.920 --> 22:02.540
I'll lend it to you.

22:02.540 --> 22:03.380
I've got 30,000.

22:03.510 --> 22:04.420
I've got 70,000.

22:04.640 --> 22:05.330
Me too.

22:05.350 --> 22:06.380
- I've got 50,000. - I've got 80,000.

22:06.830 --> 22:07.730
- I have money too.
- I'll lend you mine.

22:07.790 --> 22:08.570
We'll all lend you money.

22:08.590 --> 22:10.050
- Me too. - We'll all help.

22:11.000 --> 22:12.330
- We'll all lend you money.
- We'll all help.

22:12.400 --> 22:15.250
An auction has its rules.

22:15.880 --> 22:18.730
If people openly borrow money to keep bidding,

22:19.480 --> 22:20.460
they'll be breaking those rules.

22:21.270 --> 22:23.980
If that happens, we will hold each of you accountable.

22:24.680 --> 22:26.330
I suggest you think carefully

22:27.070 --> 22:29.900
about whether you can afford the consequences.

22:35.830 --> 22:36.570
Chief Editor Liang,

22:37.350 --> 22:40.570
do you have any additional funds to continue bidding?

22:49.110 --> 22:50.940
All we have left are the times we won in the early session.

22:51.480 --> 22:52.140
Auctioneer,

22:53.000 --> 22:56.140
can those lots from earlier be used as collateral?

23:00.440 --> 23:02.860
Since they were purchased through the Xinyue Restaurant,

23:03.960 --> 23:06.050
their authenticity and value are guaranteed.

23:07.240 --> 23:08.810
We can buy them back at the reserve price.

23:10.110 --> 23:10.660
Understood.

23:17.270 --> 23:19.250
The original purchase price of all the lots was 180,000.

23:19.480 --> 23:21.660
Based on the reserve price, their current collateral value is 108,000.

23:22.110 --> 23:23.900
The amount has now been credited to Chief Editor Liang's account.

23:28.880 --> 23:31.250
Chief Editor Liang's funds have been confirmed.

23:31.480 --> 23:32.860
The bidding may continue.

23:39.640 --> 23:41.050
All of their lots combined

23:41.750 --> 23:43.140
only cost 180,000.

23:49.270 --> 23:52.810
I bid 1.6 million.

23:53.350 --> 23:56.050
Private Room No. 1 bids 1.6 million.

24:01.070 --> 24:01.860
Chief Editor Liang,

24:02.350 --> 24:05.050
would you like to add more funds?

24:09.680 --> 24:11.900
I'll ask one last time, Chief Editor Liang.

24:12.640 --> 24:15.530
Would you like to increase your funds?

24:24.830 --> 24:26.420
I don't like a single one of today's auction items.

24:26.790 --> 24:27.770
Put them all up as collateral

24:28.000 --> 24:29.050
under Chief Editor Liang's account.

24:29.440 --> 24:30.090
Yes, Miss.

24:36.310 --> 24:38.700
Credit all the money to Mr. Liang's account.

24:42.720 --> 24:43.770
Make way!

24:43.960 --> 24:44.810
One at a time, please.

24:47.110 --> 24:47.900
Excuse me.

24:49.880 --> 24:51.240
- One at a time, please.
- Add this to Chief Editor Liang's account.

24:51.260 --> 24:52.080
- One at a time. - Thank you.

24:52.110 --> 24:52.810
One at a time.

24:54.070 --> 24:54.660
Thank you.

24:54.750 --> 24:56.860
Please credit this to Chief Editor Liang's account.

24:57.030 --> 24:58.380
- 500,000. - This is mine.

24:59.160 --> 24:59.900
Mine is 60,000.

25:00.240 --> 25:00.800
Mine.

25:00.920 --> 25:01.730
I've got it all down.

25:01.730 --> 25:05.860
[Beiping Branch of the Military Affairs Commission]

25:11.440 --> 25:12.380
No more waiting.

25:12.920 --> 25:13.700
If no one else is bidding,

25:13.880 --> 25:14.730
we can close the sale.

25:15.510 --> 25:16.530
Please wait a moment.

25:16.750 --> 25:19.530
Chief Editor Liang still has several transactions that need to be verified.

25:37.160 --> 25:37.900
Just now,

25:38.310 --> 25:40.700
many generous donors

25:40.880 --> 25:42.460
who signed as Chinese and local friends

25:43.400 --> 25:46.050
transferred funds to Chief Editor Liang's account.

25:47.640 --> 25:50.140
Chief Editor Liang, your funds are now sufficient.

25:50.440 --> 25:51.900
You may continue bidding.

25:56.160 --> 25:57.450
Find out immediately

25:57.510 --> 25:58.770
who transferred money

25:59.750 --> 26:01.170
to Liang Bencai.

26:01.590 --> 26:02.180
President,

26:02.880 --> 26:03.900
we don't have access

26:03.920 --> 26:04.900
to the Xinyue Restaurant's financial records.

26:05.200 --> 26:05.700
I'm afraid...

26:06.110 --> 26:08.380
I bid 1.65 million.

26:08.880 --> 26:10.330
Private Room No. 5

26:10.440 --> 26:11.860
bids 1.65 million.

26:12.000 --> 26:12.940
1.7 million.

26:13.000 --> 26:13.900
1.8 million.

26:13.960 --> 26:14.770
1.9 million.

26:14.960 --> 26:15.570
2 million.

26:15.680 --> 26:16.530
2.1 million.

26:16.590 --> 26:17.460
2.2 million.

26:17.590 --> 26:18.700
2.3 million.

26:18.750 --> 26:20.660
- 2.45 million. - 2.45 million.

26:21.400 --> 26:25.140
Both parties have bid 2.45 million.

26:26.400 --> 26:27.010
Will either of you

26:28.070 --> 26:30.810
raise the bid further?

26:33.830 --> 26:35.010
We're out of money.

26:35.240 --> 26:37.770
I know. Figure something out.

26:43.920 --> 26:46.460
I'll offer 200,000.

26:57.640 --> 26:59.570
The Empire of Japan and I

26:59.960 --> 27:01.290
will remember your help.

27:01.960 --> 27:04.460
Don't worry. I'll get you the antidote soon.

27:04.750 --> 27:05.810
You'll recover completely.

27:06.310 --> 27:06.940
Thank you.

27:08.000 --> 27:09.860
We need to verify the funds.

27:10.310 --> 27:10.980
I'll take it downstairs.

27:53.100 --> 27:55.340
[200,000 yuan]

27:55.790 --> 27:58.010
[200,000 yuan]
Your check was issued by the Xinyue Restaurant.

27:58.400 --> 27:59.700
It can be cashed directly.

28:01.790 --> 28:03.660
Private Room No. 1 bids...

28:03.750 --> 28:04.290
Wait.

28:06.880 --> 28:09.900
That money is for Private Room No. 5,

28:10.400 --> 28:11.660
Mr. Liang Bencai.

28:16.160 --> 28:16.810
Bravo!

28:17.830 --> 28:19.860
Bravo!

28:19.960 --> 28:21.460
Private Room No. 5 bids

28:21.680 --> 28:23.860
2.65 million, going once.

28:23.880 --> 28:24.420
Nice!

28:24.440 --> 28:26.460
2.65 million, going twice.

28:26.830 --> 28:28.940
2.65 million, going three times.

28:30.510 --> 28:31.290
Sold!

28:31.920 --> 28:35.460
- Excellent! - Bravo!

28:35.460 --> 28:37.620
- That's how it's done! - Great!

28:41.640 --> 28:43.420
The final lot of tonight's auction

28:43.480 --> 28:45.250
goes to Mr. Liang Bencai.

28:45.350 --> 28:46.570
Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang.

28:46.720 --> 28:48.700
Wonderful!

28:49.200 --> 28:52.050
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang!

28:52.110 --> 28:53.180
Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang!

28:53.200 --> 28:53.730
Great!

28:53.790 --> 28:54.460
Congratulations!

28:55.680 --> 28:57.900
Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang!

28:57.960 --> 28:59.770
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations, Chief Editor Liang!

29:05.960 --> 29:07.420
Without our antidote,

29:08.000 --> 29:09.730
she won't survive this month.

29:14.270 --> 29:17.490
Allow me to introduce the adviser I invited for this auction.

29:21.110 --> 29:21.810
Chief Editor Liang,

29:22.790 --> 29:23.380
I've heard a great deal about you.

29:24.240 --> 29:25.660
He's not Liang Bencai.

29:28.550 --> 29:31.250
He must've known Huo Xiangu all along.

29:34.440 --> 29:35.090
Go look into it.

29:36.350 --> 29:38.140
Start with the people around Huo Xiangu.

29:38.160 --> 29:39.470
Check every single one of them.

29:39.510 --> 29:39.980
Yes, sir.

29:42.270 --> 29:43.700
Those people from the magazine

29:44.440 --> 29:46.330
actually conspired with them to deceive us.

29:48.880 --> 29:51.380
Lackeys will always be lackeys.

29:53.030 --> 29:54.050
They can never be truly loyal.

29:55.790 --> 29:57.860
Wipe them all out.

29:58.440 --> 29:59.810
Leave no one behind.

30:00.110 --> 30:00.530
Yes, sir.

30:02.790 --> 30:05.770
Mobilize everyone we can.

30:06.350 --> 30:09.660
No matter what happens tonight, no one is leaving with that chest.

30:11.030 --> 30:14.770
I'll take responsibility for whatever chaos follows.

30:15.070 --> 30:15.530
Yes, sir.

30:20.640 --> 30:21.700
Mr. Tottori,

30:22.240 --> 30:24.860
we've always advocated maintaining friendly relations between our two countries.

30:25.590 --> 30:27.220
Perhaps

30:27.240 --> 30:28.700
there has been some misunderstanding.

30:28.830 --> 30:30.250
Misunderstanding or not,

30:30.590 --> 30:31.900
that's for us to decide.

30:32.960 --> 30:35.330
I demand that you immediately seal off the premises

30:35.790 --> 30:37.140
and detain everyone involved.

30:43.030 --> 30:43.420
Mr. Yin,

30:43.880 --> 30:44.730
the Japanese are mobilizing soldiers

30:44.750 --> 30:45.900
from the Military Affairs Commission

30:46.200 --> 30:47.700
to lock down the entire building and interrogate everyone present.

30:48.350 --> 30:48.900
Clear the building.

30:49.270 --> 30:50.530
Escort all the guests out immediately.

30:50.720 --> 30:51.250
No mistakes.

30:51.440 --> 30:51.900
Yes, sir.

30:52.880 --> 30:53.330
Move!

30:53.350 --> 30:53.770
Hurry!

30:53.830 --> 30:55.980
No one leaves!

30:57.790 --> 30:58.900
Who gave you permission to go?

31:00.140 --> 31:00.750
This way!

31:01.480 --> 31:02.040
Keep moving.

31:02.200 --> 31:03.040
The Japanese soldiers are here!

31:03.040 --> 31:03.570
Run!

31:05.240 --> 31:06.250
Darn it!

31:07.030 --> 31:09.090
President, everyone's gone.

31:10.110 --> 31:10.770
Those ear slaves

31:10.790 --> 31:12.640
actually pressed their ears against my door

31:12.880 --> 31:14.660
and secretly let everyone escape.

31:17.070 --> 31:20.460
The Xinyue Restaurant has ruined the Empire's plans.

31:21.000 --> 31:22.380
Should we make a move against them?

31:24.720 --> 31:26.980
If the Military Affairs Commission weren't protecting them,

31:27.480 --> 31:29.860
I'd have flattened this place tonight.

31:35.240 --> 31:36.330
Let's head back first.

31:59.680 --> 32:00.140
Master Zhang.

32:00.480 --> 32:00.940
Xinyue.

32:01.310 --> 32:01.940
You're here.

32:03.830 --> 32:05.570
Young Lady, this is as far as we can escort you.

32:05.880 --> 32:07.250
The Xinyue Restaurant is a neutral establishment.

32:07.510 --> 32:09.330
By our rules, we can't interfere with where the goods go next.

32:10.830 --> 32:12.220
The Japanese won't let this go.

32:12.640 --> 32:13.860
I need to go back and deal with the aftermath.

32:14.550 --> 32:15.660
Will you be alright?

32:16.270 --> 32:17.380
Don't worry about me.

32:18.160 --> 32:19.700
The Xinyue Restaurant has stood for over a century.

32:20.000 --> 32:21.220
We've weathered every storm imaginable.

32:22.240 --> 32:23.330
We'll handle it.

32:24.960 --> 32:25.700
As for you,

32:26.920 --> 32:28.490
you're taking something that large out of the city.

32:29.550 --> 32:30.770
Whatever you do, don't get caught.

32:31.400 --> 32:31.940
Alright?

32:35.440 --> 32:37.420
Don't worry. I know what I'm doing.

32:43.750 --> 32:44.250
Let's go.

32:58.070 --> 32:59.460
Master Zhang, Xiangu...

32:59.960 --> 33:01.330
She has her reasons she can't tell us.

33:03.920 --> 33:04.530
What's happening?

33:04.830 --> 33:05.530
On the way here,

33:05.680 --> 33:07.290
we saw armed Japanese everywhere.

33:07.720 --> 33:09.490
They've set up roadblocks through several blocks. There's no way out.

33:11.400 --> 33:12.490
Master Zhang, what do we do?

33:16.030 --> 33:16.660
Force our way through.

33:22.920 --> 33:23.700
Split up and look for them.

33:24.000 --> 33:24.660
Yes, sir.

33:26.350 --> 33:26.810
Move.

34:00.830 --> 34:01.620
There they are!

34:01.920 --> 34:03.250
Take them and the chest!

34:03.510 --> 34:03.980
Xiaoyu,

34:04.310 --> 34:05.700
take Tiezui and Jiu back.

34:05.880 --> 34:06.730
- Now. - Yes, sir.

34:07.960 --> 34:08.900
Nobody move!

34:17.590 --> 34:18.490
Mr. Liang,

34:19.360 --> 34:20.690
come with us.

34:42.710 --> 34:46.460
Mr. Liang, long time no see.

34:47.550 --> 34:48.610
Please get in.

34:49.150 --> 34:51.010
I'll take you to the train station.

34:53.880 --> 34:55.900
You forgot me already, my friend?

34:56.710 --> 34:57.340
My goodness.

34:59.630 --> 35:01.490
The owner of the Xinyue Restaurant asked me to come.

35:01.510 --> 35:02.490
What are you doing?

35:04.150 --> 35:05.010
Step aside.

35:05.510 --> 35:07.570
We're carrying out official duties.

35:11.000 --> 35:12.340
Mr. Liang is an expert

35:12.360 --> 35:14.260
invited by the American Chamber of Commerce.

35:15.480 --> 35:16.740
I have a travel permit.

35:16.740 --> 35:17.420
[Travel Permit]

35:20.710 --> 35:22.820
He's our guest tonight.

35:23.280 --> 35:24.010
He's not under your jurisdiction.

35:24.070 --> 35:24.490
That's right.

35:25.150 --> 35:26.050
Not your concern.

35:26.670 --> 35:28.490
They're criminals.

35:30.030 --> 35:31.170
They incited anti-Japanese sentiment

35:31.760 --> 35:32.690
and provoked the Empire.

35:33.840 --> 35:36.340
They must stay.

35:37.110 --> 35:38.380
Take a good look.

35:39.110 --> 35:41.900
This is a vehicle from the US Consulate.

35:44.960 --> 35:46.170
If you stop this car and arrest these people,

35:46.190 --> 35:48.380
you'll be interfering in American affairs.

35:49.510 --> 35:51.740
Trying to trigger a diplomatic incident between Japan and the United States?

35:52.760 --> 35:55.490
Or is Japan declaring war on America?

36:00.670 --> 36:02.010
Please get in.

36:05.440 --> 36:06.300
Come with me.

36:23.000 --> 36:24.260
Darn it!

36:25.820 --> 36:26.590
[Special Execution Order]

36:26.590 --> 36:27.340
Mr. Tottori,

36:27.630 --> 36:28.690
we've received an order from our superiors

36:29.000 --> 36:30.530
to fully cooperate with your operation.

36:35.880 --> 36:37.300
They've all escaped.

36:37.510 --> 36:38.940
What use are you now?

36:39.960 --> 36:41.340
We're only following orders.

36:41.840 --> 36:43.980
Is there anything else you'd like us to do?

36:46.960 --> 36:47.570
Get out.

36:48.400 --> 36:49.170
Out!

37:20.000 --> 37:21.610
I knew you'd come back.

37:22.440 --> 37:23.420
Because only I

37:24.280 --> 37:25.380
can cure you.

37:26.400 --> 37:27.210
Give me the antidote.

37:51.360 --> 37:53.530
I hate being lied to.

37:54.710 --> 37:56.490
Especially by someone I care about.

37:57.400 --> 37:59.900
You'll have plenty of time to find out

38:00.440 --> 38:01.780
what happens

38:02.960 --> 38:04.690
to people who deceive me.

38:08.190 --> 38:09.010
Guards.

38:10.960 --> 38:12.260
Take her away.

38:12.880 --> 38:14.130
I'll interrogate her personally.

38:15.400 --> 38:16.050
Wait.

38:20.670 --> 38:22.050
The building has been cleared.

38:22.960 --> 38:24.340
Why are you still here?

38:32.960 --> 38:34.090
You're coming home with me.

38:35.320 --> 38:35.940
Stop.

38:37.110 --> 38:38.130
She's a suspect.

38:38.630 --> 38:40.340
She must be interrogated.

38:41.400 --> 38:42.380
On what charge?

38:42.590 --> 38:43.980
She incited anti-Japanese sentiment

38:44.920 --> 38:46.490
at tonight's auction.

38:48.070 --> 38:49.340
Isn't that enough?

38:50.070 --> 38:51.130
What exactly did she say?

38:53.320 --> 38:54.490
We'll know after we question her.

38:54.630 --> 38:56.050
So you have no charge

38:56.080 --> 38:57.010
and no proof.

38:59.840 --> 39:01.340
She's an employee of the Xinyue Restaurant.

39:02.110 --> 39:03.650
She wasn't part of the auction.

39:04.000 --> 39:05.340
She's outside your jurisdiction.

39:05.360 --> 39:06.610
I have a warrant.

39:08.840 --> 39:11.490
I'm authorized to detain anyone suspicious.

39:13.440 --> 39:14.740
Is the Xinyue Restaurant

39:15.960 --> 39:17.490
trying to shield her?

39:18.440 --> 39:20.210
You can't make baseless accusations like that.

39:20.920 --> 39:21.690
Let me tell you this.

39:22.550 --> 39:24.380
She's not only an employee of the Xinyue Restaurant,

39:25.440 --> 39:27.050
but she's also my goddaughter.

39:27.760 --> 39:29.900
I won't allow anyone

39:30.000 --> 39:31.170
to bully her.

39:31.630 --> 39:33.090
Everyone knows

39:33.630 --> 39:34.780
the Xinyue Restaurant

39:36.070 --> 39:38.380
is an officially designated trading house of the Central Government,

39:38.550 --> 39:39.900
under the protection of the Ministry of War.

39:40.920 --> 39:43.460
That piece of paper means nothing here.

39:44.550 --> 39:45.050
Stop.

39:45.150 --> 39:45.610
Come.

39:46.190 --> 39:46.650
Let's go home.

39:47.190 --> 39:47.780
Stop!

39:48.960 --> 39:50.570
I said stop!

39:52.070 --> 39:52.860
Mr. Tottori,

39:53.360 --> 39:54.530
your warrant

39:55.000 --> 39:57.380
does not authorize action against Xinyue Restaurant personnel.

39:57.670 --> 39:59.170
We have no authority to touch her.

40:00.070 --> 40:01.460
You...

40:03.880 --> 40:04.420
President.

40:06.960 --> 40:08.090
Did we get the chest back?

40:08.510 --> 40:10.130
The chest and Liang Bencai

40:11.000 --> 40:12.460
were taken away

40:12.920 --> 40:13.860
by the people from the American Chamber of Commerce.

40:14.110 --> 40:14.900
Darn it!

40:15.880 --> 40:17.380
How are the Americans involved now?

40:18.150 --> 40:19.860
Who are these people?

40:20.960 --> 40:22.010
What about the other chest?

40:22.960 --> 40:24.130
We still don't know.

40:24.400 --> 40:26.170
But I've given the order.

40:26.920 --> 40:27.940
No matter the cost,

40:28.190 --> 40:28.900
we must seize it.

40:45.860 --> 40:48.340
[Xinyue Restaurant Collection Receipt]

40:50.840 --> 40:52.650
Now everyone in Beiping

40:53.110 --> 40:55.090
knows my name.

41:30.190 --> 41:31.650
If you want to pass through here,

41:32.190 --> 41:33.650
pay your toll.

41:34.510 --> 41:35.980
You little punk.

41:36.550 --> 41:38.260
When I was running guns and cargo,

41:38.510 --> 41:40.090
you were still wetting your pants and playing in the mud.

41:40.630 --> 41:42.460
Men, get him!

42:26.280 --> 42:27.260
Mr. Tian.

42:28.320 --> 42:29.260
Black Bear?

42:29.960 --> 42:30.900
No wonder.

42:31.400 --> 42:32.940
The moment I left the auction,

42:33.030 --> 42:34.300
you'd be waiting to ambush me.

42:34.840 --> 42:36.900
Cripple him!

42:37.320 --> 42:38.380
If he dies, I'll take the blame.

42:38.480 --> 42:39.050
Yes, sir.

42:54.710 --> 42:56.860
Kill them. Take the chest.

42:57.440 --> 42:58.300
The Japanese.

43:11.710 --> 43:12.780
Watch your back.

43:58.070 --> 43:58.900
Are you alright?

44:00.440 --> 44:01.210
Go.

44:01.630 --> 44:02.460
Take the chest.

44:02.840 --> 44:04.210
China's treasures

44:04.760 --> 44:06.260
must never fall into Japanese hands.

44:07.110 --> 44:07.820
Don't worry.

44:08.920 --> 44:10.820
Bring it on, you punk.

44:21.280 --> 44:22.650
Boss, we can't beat them.

44:22.760 --> 44:23.420
We should run.

44:24.630 --> 44:25.340
Run?

44:25.880 --> 44:26.780
This is China.

44:27.190 --> 44:28.170
They're the ones who should leave.

44:28.440 --> 44:30.260
Help them get the chest.

44:30.510 --> 44:31.260
Beat the Japanese.

44:31.480 --> 44:32.340
Boss, but...

44:32.630 --> 44:33.380
Now!

44:33.840 --> 44:34.340
Yes, sir.

45:55.260 --> 45:59.420
♪The past fades like smoke♪

45:59.780 --> 46:02.500
♪A choice is made in silence♪

46:02.780 --> 46:05.580
♪In this labyrinthine puzzle♪

